{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2484 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "48cc9c8fc998188a2815d6e3c52003882ed02b490b3ed8263fadefebad15c72c" :edb/db-before-t 2483 :edb/db-after-t 2484 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535796 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:22:36.088Z" 13194139535796 true] [17592186078414 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366656 13194139535796 true] [17592186078414 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366670 13194139535796 true] [17592186078415 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366663 13194139535796 true] [17592186079077 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535796 true] [17592186079077 1100 "Given that $y = y(t)$ satisfies the equation $y^{″} + 3y^{′} - 4y = 0$, which of the following **cannot** be $y(t)$?" 13194139535796 false] [17592186079077 1100 "Given that $y=y(t)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}-4y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(t)?$" 13194139535796 true] [17592186079077 1145 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-4{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-4$ or $\\lambda =1.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-4t}$ and ${e}^{t}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{-t}$ is not a solution." 13194139535796 true] [17592186079121 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535796 true] [17592186079121 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+8y=0.\n$$" 13194139535796 true] [17592186079121 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} + 6\\frac{dy}{dx} + 8y = 0$." 13194139535796 false] [17592186079121 1145 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +4)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =-4.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366656 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366657 13194139535796 true] [17592186366656 1089 "q-130118" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366656 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535796 true] [17592186366656 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=0.\n$$" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366656 1113 #uuid "423c3716-190e-5b6f-9635-03a5ec2b0925" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366656 1145 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-5\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =1$ or $\\lambda =4.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{4x}.\n$$" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366658 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366659 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366660 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366661 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366662 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1041 "selection" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366661 13194139535796 true] [17592186366657 1110 #uuid "d3fb6eb3-577e-5782-86b5-8fbd4c870479" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366658 1034 "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{x}" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535796 true] [17592186366658 1111 #uuid "dd0e14a7-1831-52de-b97d-f9bbca01cb51" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366659 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{5x}" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535796 true] [17592186366659 1111 #uuid "03b8a4eb-5926-5b39-838c-eb42edb068fe" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366660 1034 "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{5x}" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535796 true] [17592186366660 1111 #uuid "95106564-a137-582a-b583-d1be407d85f3" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366661 1034 "y=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{4x}" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535796 true] [17592186366661 1111 #uuid "866058ed-b3a2-5418-ac4f-ca1999de2e8b" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366662 1034 "y=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{4x}" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535796 true] [17592186366662 1111 #uuid "0e0556aa-9b10-5ae0-8448-b3a93b10d052" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366663 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366664 13194139535796 true] [17592186366663 1089 "q-64706" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366663 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535796 true] [17592186366663 1100 "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-3y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366663 1113 #uuid "670e5717-fad8-5791-a10e-1498d79849c5" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366663 1145 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -3)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =3.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-x}$ and ${e}^{3x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-5{e}^{-3x}$ is not a solution." 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366665 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366666 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366667 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366668 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366669 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1041 "selection" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366667 13194139535796 true] [17592186366664 1110 #uuid "b48aa4a7-b1fc-5bff-9c8a-c84ab1e6c7ba" 13194139535796 true] [17592186366665 1034 "2{e}^{-x}+